<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada intervenes to add liquidity.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada intervenes to add liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada conducted on Thursday a round of special purchase and resale agreements at 3.25 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>The central bank intervened to add liquidity to the money market after Canada's call loan rate was trading at 3.25 percent, a trader said. The bank's floor for the range is 2.75 percent.</p>
<p>After the intervention, the call loan rate was still trading at around 3.25 percent, the trader said.</p>
<p>((Paul Simao, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8104))</p>
